<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply off $12.6 bln in May 5 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply off $12.6 bln in May 5 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply fell $12.6 billion in the May 5 week to $3,894.4 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure fell $15.8 billion to $5,048.1 billion. M-1 fell $700 million to $1,064.1 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,903.5 billion versus $3,904.2 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
